TITLE:: PathActionQMenu
summary:: A Button with a popup Menu for performing actions on file paths.
categories:: GUI>Views, Libraries>jostMlib
related:: jostMlib,  Classes/ActionQMenu, Classes/ActionMenu, Classes/PathActionMenu, Classes/Menu, Classes/MenuAction

DESCRIPTION::
An ActionQMenu, where string entries are interpreted as file/folder paths.
A folder works multi-level, listing subfolders.

You can still add \key->action associations, just like in ActionMenu.

Closes on click outside or on escape key.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create an ActionMenu

ARGUMENT:: parent
The parent view.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
A Rect

ARGUMENT:: name
The Menu Button Title

ARGUMENT:: items
An Array of Strings or Associations (\key->function)

Strings ar interpreted as FilePaths

ARGUMENT:: preload
default: defaultPreload. Preload the submenus. Makes menu items more respnsive.  Caution: can slow things down with large directories.

ARGUMENT:: showArrow
show a little down-tick arrow, defaults to true

returns::
an ActionQMenu


METHOD:: defaultAllowedFiles
Default: ["rtf","rtfd","sc","scd","html","HTML","schelp"]

METHOD:: defaultOpenAction
a default function you can set for all  items.

{|path,modifier,buttonNum| doSomething()}

METHOD:: defaultPreload
default: true. Preload the submenus. Makes menu items more respnsive.  Caution: can slow things down with large directories.


INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: allowedFiles
Default: ["rtf","rtfd","sc","scd","html","HTML","schelp"]


METHOD:: openAction
a function run on the selected path. Typically open a file.

{|path,modifier,buttonNum| doSomething()}

You can set it on the instance, or you can set a default with  PathActionMenu.defaultOpenAction


PRIVATE:: prAddItem
PRIVATE:: prFileItem
PRIVATE:: prFolderItem
PRIVATE:: prPathItem
PRIVATE:: prPathUp
PRIVATE:: openfunction
PRIVATE:: prButtonAction
PRIVATE:: prRefreshAction
PRIVATE:: prPopulateSubmenu
PRIVATE:: prHandleString
PRIVATE:: addItem
PRIVATE:: returnpaths

EXAMPLES::

code::
(
// Make sure the paths are present, or they will be ignored.
// Associations work like ActionMenu.
// Strings are interpreted as file or directory paths.
// File paths directly run the openAction.
// Directories navigate to the next level with a new window and an up (../) option.
// argumentsfor  openAction and defaultOpenAction are  path,modifier,buttonNum .

w = Window.new("PathActionMenu Examples").front;
w.flow{arg w;
    var m;
    m=PathActionQMenu(w,Rect(0,0,150,25),"Open Files and Dirs",[
        \testMe->{|path,modifier,buttonNum|[path,modifier,buttonNum].postln}, // an association with a custom action
        Association("*testMe 2*",{|path,modifier,buttonNum|[path,modifier,buttonNum].postln}), // an long keyed association with a custom action
        "~/Documents/",
        "~/Shared/",
		Platform.userAppSupportDir++"/startup.scd",
		"-",
		Platform.userAppSupportDir++"/*", // '*' will iterate over the dir on the top level

    ],preload: false); // some directories are huge, so we need to lazy load them
    m.openAction= {|path,modifier,buttonNum|
        [path,modifier,buttonNum].postln;
        Document.open(path);
        // Or use your custom editor
        // ("open -a  Sublime\\ Text "++path.escapeChar($ )).unixCmd;
    };

    w.startRow;
    StaticText(w,Rect(0,0,200,40)).string_("Click outside to close.");
    w.startRow;
    StaticText(w,Rect(0,0,200,40)).string_("Escape key  to close.");


};


)

//You can also create a directory of files containing
{arg v; "myFunc".postln}; // example
// and then set the openAction to

m.openAction= {|path|path.load.value(v)};
// In this way you can separate your code functions into many small files.


::
